---Specifies an alarm and associates it with the specified metric or metric math expression.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsCloudWatchAlarmDetails
---@field ActionsEnabled? aws.securityhub.Boolean Indicates whether actions should be executed during any changes to the alarm state.
---@field AlarmActions? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyStringList The list of actions, specified as Amazon Resource Names (ARNs) to execute when this alarm transitions into an ALARM state from any other state.
---@field AlarmArn? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The ARN of the alarm.
---@field AlarmConfigurationUpdatedTimestamp? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The time stamp of the last update to the alarm configuration.
---@field AlarmDescription? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The description of the alarm.
---@field AlarmName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the alarm. If you don't specify a name, CloudFront generates a unique physical ID and uses that ID for the alarm name.
---@field ComparisonOperator? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The arithmetic operation to use when comparing the specified statistic and threshold. The specified statistic value is used as the first operand.
---@field DatapointsToAlarm? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of datapoints that must be breaching to trigger the alarm.
---@field Dimensions? aws.securityhub.AwsCloudWatchAlarmDimensionsList The dimensions for the metric associated with the alarm.
---@field EvaluateLowSampleCountPercentile? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Used only for alarms based on percentiles. If ignore, the alarm state does not change during periods with too few data points to be statistically significant. If evaluate or this parameter is not used, the alarm is always evaluated and possibly changes state no matter how many data points are available.
---@field EvaluationPeriods? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of periods over which data is compared to the specified threshold.
---@field ExtendedStatistic? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The percentile statistic for the metric associated with the alarm.
---@field InsufficientDataActions? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyStringList The actions to execute when this alarm transitions to the INSUFFICIENT_DATA state from any other state. Each action is specified as an ARN.
---@field MetricName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the metric associated with the alarm. This is required for an alarm based on a metric. For an alarm based on a math expression, you use Metrics instead and you can't specify MetricName.
---@field Namespace? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The namespace of the metric associated with the alarm. This is required for an alarm based on a metric. For an alarm based on a math expression, you can't specify Namespace and you use Metrics instead.
---@field OkActions? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyStringList The actions to execute when this alarm transitions to the OK state from any other state. Each action is specified as an ARN.
---@field Period? aws.securityhub.Integer The period, in seconds, over which the statistic is applied. This is required for an alarm based on a metric.
---@field Statistic? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The statistic for the metric associated with the alarm, other than percentile. For percentile statistics, use ExtendedStatistic.
---@field Threshold? aws.securityhub.Double The value to compare with the specified statistic.
---@field ThresholdMetricId? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString n an alarm based on an anomaly detection model, this is the ID of the ANOMALY_DETECTION_BAND function used as the threshold for the alarm.
---@field TreatMissingData? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Sets how this alarm is to handle missing data points.
---@field Unit? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The unit of the metric associated with the alarm.

---Details about the dimensions for the metric associated with the alarm.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsCloudWatchAlarmDimensionsDetails
---@field Name? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of a dimension.
---@field Value? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The value of a dimension.

---@alias aws.securityhub.AwsCloudWatchAlarmDimensionsList aws.securityhub.AwsCloudWatchAlarmDimensionsDetails[]

