---@field KmsKeyId? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString An DMS key identifier that is used to encrypt the connection parameters for the endpoint. If you don't specify a value for the KmsKeyId parameter, then DMS uses your default encryption key. KMS creates the default encryption key for your Amazon Web Services account. Your Amazon Web Services account has a different default encryption key for each Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field Port? aws.securityhub.Integer The port used to access the endpoint.
---@field ServerName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the server where the endpoint database resides.
---@field SslMode? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The SSL mode used to connect to the endpoint. The default is none.
---@field Username? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The user name to be used to log in to the endpoint database.

---Provides details about an Database Migration Service (DMS) replication instance. DMS uses a replication instance to connect to your source data store, read the source data, and format the data for consumption by the target data store.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsDmsReplicationInstanceDetails
---@field AllocatedStorage? aws.securityhub.Integer The amount of storage (in gigabytes) that is allocated for the replication instance.
---@field AutoMinorVersionUpgrade? aws.securityhub.Boolean Indicates whether minor engine upgrades are applied automatically to the replication instance during the maintenance window.
---@field AvailabilityZone? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The Availability Zone that the replication instance is created in. The default value is a random, system-chosen Availability Zone in the endpoint's Amazon Web Services Region, such as us-east-1d.
---@field EngineVersion? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The engine version number of the replication instance. If an engine version number is not specified when a replication instance is created, the default is the latest engine version available.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString An KMS key identifier that is used to encrypt the data on the replication instance. If you don't specify a value for the KmsKeyId parameter, DMS uses your default encryption key. KMS creates the default encryption key for your Amazon Web Services account. Your Amazon Web Services account has a different default encryption key for each Amazon Web Services Region.
---@field MultiAZ? aws.securityhub.Boolean Specifies whether the replication instance is deployed across multiple Availability Zones (AZs). You can't set the AvailabilityZone parameter if the MultiAZ parameter is set to true.
---@field PreferredMaintenanceWindow? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The maintenance window times for the replication instance. Upgrades to the replication instance are performed during this time.
---@field PubliclyAccessible? aws.securityhub.Boolean Specifies the accessibility options for the replication instance. A value of true represents an instance with a public IP address. A value of false represents an instance with a private IP address. The default value is true.
---@field ReplicationInstanceClass? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The compute and memory capacity of the replication instance as defined for the specified replication instance class.
---@field ReplicationInstanceIdentifier? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The replication instance identifier.
---@field ReplicationSubnetGroup? aws.securityhub.AwsDmsReplicationInstanceReplicationSubnetGroupDetails The subnet group for the replication instance.
---@field VpcSecurityGroups? aws.securityhub.AwsDmsReplicationInstanceVpcSecurityGroupsList The virtual private cloud (VPC) security group for the replication instance.

