---@field Essential? aws.securityhub.Boolean Whether the container is essential. All tasks must have at least one essential container.
---@field ExtraHosts? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsExtraHostsList A list of hostnames and IP address mappings to append to the /etc/hosts file on the container.
---@field FirelensConfiguration? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsFirelensConfigurationDetails The FireLens configuration for the container. Specifies and configures a log router for container logs.
---@field HealthCheck? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsHealthCheckDetails The container health check command and associated configuration parameters for the container.
---@field Hostname? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The hostname to use for the container.
---@field Image? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The image used to start the container.
---@field Interactive? aws.securityhub.Boolean If set to true, then containerized applications can be deployed that require stdin or a tty to be allocated.
---@field Links? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyStringList A list of links for the container in the form container_name:alias . Allows containers to communicate with each other without the need for port mappings.
---@field LinuxParameters? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsLinuxParametersDetails Linux-specific modifications that are applied to the container, such as Linux kernel capabilities.
---@field LogConfiguration? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsLogConfigurationDetails The log configuration specification for the container.
---@field Memory? aws.securityhub.Integer The amount (in MiB) of memory to present to the container. If the container attempts to exceed the memory specified here, the container is shut down. The total amount of memory reserved for all containers within a task must be lower than the task memory value, if one is specified.
---@field MemoryReservation? aws.securityhub.Integer The soft limit (in MiB) of memory to reserve for the container.
---@field MountPoints? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsMountPointsList The mount points for the data volumes in the container.
---@field Name? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the container.
---@field PortMappings? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsPortMappingsList The list of port mappings for the container.
---@field Privileged? aws.securityhub.Boolean Whether the container is given elevated privileges on the host container instance. The elevated privileges are similar to the root user.
---@field PseudoTerminal? aws.securityhub.Boolean Whether to allocate a TTY to the container.
---@field ReadonlyRootFilesystem? aws.securityhub.Boolean Whether the container is given read-only access to its root file system.
---@field RepositoryCredentials? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsRepositoryCredentialsDetails The private repository authentication credentials to use.
---@field ResourceRequirements? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsResourceRequirementsList The type and amount of a resource to assign to a container. The only supported resource is a GPU.
---@field Secrets? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsSecretsList The secrets to pass to the container.
---@field StartTimeout? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of seconds to wait before giving up on resolving dependencies for a container.
---@field StopTimeout? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of seconds to wait before the container is stopped if it doesn't shut down normally on its own.
---@field SystemControls? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsSystemControlsList A list of namespaced kernel parameters to set in the container.
---@field Ulimits? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsUlimitsList A list of ulimits to set in the container.
---@field User? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The user to use inside the container.
---@field VolumesFrom? aws.securityhub.AwsEcsTaskDefinitionContainerDefinitionsVolumesFromList Data volumes to mount from another container.
---@field WorkingDirectory? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The working directory in which to run commands inside the container.

