---details about the configuration of an OpenSearch cluster.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsElasticsearchDomainElasticsearchClusterConfigDetails
---@field DedicatedMasterCount? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of instances to use for the master node. If this attribute is specified, then DedicatedMasterEnabled must be true.
---@field DedicatedMasterEnabled? aws.securityhub.Boolean Whether to use a dedicated master node for the Elasticsearch domain. A dedicated master node performs cluster management tasks, but doesn't hold data or respond to data upload requests.
---@field DedicatedMasterType? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The hardware configuration of the computer that hosts the dedicated master node. A sample value is m3.medium.elasticsearch. If this attribute is specified, then DedicatedMasterEnabled must be true.
---@field InstanceCount? aws.securityhub.Integer The number of data nodes to use in the Elasticsearch domain.
