---Provides a consistent format for Security Hub CSPM findings. AwsSecurityFinding format allows you to share findings between Amazon Web Services security services and third-party solutions.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsSecurityFinding
---@field SchemaVersion aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The schema version that a finding is formatted for. The value is 2018-10-08.
---@field Id aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The security findings provider-specific identifier for a finding.
---@field ProductArn aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The ARN generated by Security Hub CSPM that uniquely identifies a product that generates findings. This can be the ARN for a third-party product that is integrated with Security Hub CSPM, or the ARN for a custom integration.
---@field ProductName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the product that generated the finding.
---@field CompanyName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the company for the product that generated the finding.
---@field Region? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The Region from which the finding was generated.
---@field GeneratorId aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The identifier for the solution-specific component (a discrete unit of logic) that generated a finding. In various security findings providers' solutions, this generator can be called a rule, a check, a detector, a plugin, or something else.
---@field AwsAccountId aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The Amazon Web Services account ID that a finding is generated in.
---@field Types? aws.securityhub.TypeList One or more finding types in the format of namespace/category/classifier that classify a finding.
---@field FirstObservedAt? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Indicates when the security findings provider first observed the potential security issue that a finding captured.
---@field LastObservedAt? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Indicates when the security findings provider most recently observed a change in the resource that is involved in the finding.
---@field CreatedAt aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Indicates when the security findings provider created the potential security issue that a finding captured.
---@field UpdatedAt aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString Indicates when the security findings provider last updated the finding record.
---@field Severity? aws.securityhub.Severity A finding's severity.
---@field Confidence? aws.securityhub.Integer A finding's confidence. Confidence is defined as the likelihood that a finding accurately identifies the behavior or issue that it was intended to identify.
---@field Criticality? aws.securityhub.Integer The level of importance assigned to the resources associated with the finding.
---@field Title aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString A finding's title. Title is a required property.
---@field Description aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString A finding's description. Description is a required property.
---@field Remediation? aws.securityhub.Remediation A data type that describes the remediation options for a finding.
---@field SourceUrl? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString A URL that links to a page about the current finding in the security findings provider's solution.
---@field ProductFields? aws.securityhub.FieldMap A data type where security findings providers can include additional solution-specific details that aren't part of the defined AwsSecurityFinding format.
---@field UserDefinedFields? aws.securityhub.FieldMap A list of name/value string pairs associated with the finding. These are custom, user-defined fields added to a finding.
---@field Malware? aws.securityhub.MalwareList A list of malware related to a finding.
---@field Network? aws.securityhub.Network The details of network-related information about a finding.
---@field NetworkPath? aws.securityhub.NetworkPathList Provides information about a network path that is relevant to a finding. Each entry under NetworkPath represents a component of that path.
---@field Process? aws.securityhub.ProcessDetails The details of process-related information about a finding.
---@field Threats? aws.securityhub.ThreatList Details about the threat detected in a security finding and the file paths that were affected by the threat.
---@field ThreatIntelIndicators? aws.securityhub.ThreatIntelIndicatorList Threat intelligence details related to a finding.
---@field Resources aws.securityhub.ResourceList A set of resource data types that describe the resources that the finding refers to.
---@field Compliance? aws.securityhub.Compliance This data type is exclusive to findings that are generated as the result of a check run against a specific rule in a supported security standard, such as CIS Amazon Web Services Foundations. Contains security standard-related finding details.
---@field VerificationState? aws.securityhub.VerificationState|string Indicates the veracity of a finding.
---@field WorkflowState? aws.securityhub.WorkflowState|string The workflow state of a finding.
---@field Workflow? aws.securityhub.Workflow Provides information about the status of the investigation into a finding.
---@field RecordState? aws.securityhub.RecordState|string The record state of a finding.
---@field RelatedFindings? aws.securityhub.RelatedFindingList A list of related findings.
---@field Note? aws.securityhub.Note A user-defined note added to a finding.
---@field Vulnerabilities? aws.securityhub.VulnerabilityList Provides a list of vulnerabilities associated with the findings.
---@field PatchSummary? aws.securityhub.PatchSummary Provides an overview of the patch compliance status for an instance against a selected compliance standard.
---@field Action? aws.securityhub.Action Provides details about an action that affects or that was taken on a resource.
---@field FindingProviderFields? aws.securityhub.FindingProviderFields In a BatchImportFindings request, finding providers use FindingProviderFields to provide and update their own values for confidence, criticality, related findings, severity, and types.
---@field Sample? aws.securityhub.Boolean Indicates whether the finding is a sample finding.
---@field GeneratorDetails? aws.securityhub.GeneratorDetails Provides metadata for the Amazon CodeGuru detector associated with a finding. This field pertains to findings that relate to Lambda functions. Amazon Inspector identifies policy violations and vulnerabilities in Lambda function code based on internal detectors developed in collaboration with Amazon CodeGuru. Security Hub CSPM receives those findings.
---@field ProcessedAt? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString A timestamp that indicates when Security Hub CSPM received a finding and begins to process it.
---@field AwsAccountName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the Amazon Web Services account from which a finding was generated.
---@field Detection? aws.securityhub.Detection Provides details about an Amazon GuardDuty Extended Threat Detection attack sequence. GuardDuty generates an attack sequence finding when multiple events align to a potentially suspicious activity. To receive GuardDuty attack sequence findings in Security Hub CSPM, you must have GuardDuty enabled. For more information, see GuardDuty Extended Threat Detection in the Amazon GuardDuty User Guide.

---A collection of filters that are applied to all active findings aggregated by Security Hub CSPM.
---@class aws.securityhub.AwsSecurityFindingFilters
---@field ProductArn? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The ARN generated by Security Hub CSPM that uniquely identifies a third-party company (security findings provider) after this provider's product (solution that generates findings) is registered with Security Hub CSPM.
---@field AwsAccountId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The Amazon Web Services account ID in which a finding is generated.
---@field Id? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The security findings provider-specific identifier for a finding.
---@field GeneratorId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The identifier for the solution-specific component (a discrete unit of logic) that generated a finding. In various security findings providers' solutions, this generator can be called a rule, a check, a detector, a plugin, etc.
---@field Region? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The Region from which the finding was generated.
---@field Type? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList A finding type in the format of namespace/category/classifier that classifies a finding.
---@field FirstObservedAt? aws.securityhub.DateFilterList A timestamp that indicates when the security findings provider first observed the potential security issue that a finding captured.
---@field LastObservedAt? aws.securityhub.DateFilterList A timestamp that indicates when the security findings provider most recently observed a change in the resource that is involved in the finding.
---@field CreatedAt? aws.securityhub.DateFilterList A timestamp that indicates when the security findings provider created the potential security issue that a finding reflects.
---@field UpdatedAt? aws.securityhub.DateFilterList A timestamp that indicates when the security findings provider last updated the finding record.
---@field SeverityProduct? aws.securityhub.NumberFilterList The native severity as defined by the security findings provider's solution that generated the finding.
---@field SeverityNormalized? aws.securityhub.NumberFilterList The normalized severity of a finding.
---@field SeverityLabel? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The label of a finding's severity.
---@field Confidence? aws.securityhub.NumberFilterList A finding's confidence. Confidence is defined as the likelihood that a finding accurately identifies the behavior or issue that it was intended to identify.
---@field Criticality? aws.securityhub.NumberFilterList The level of importance assigned to the resources associated with the finding.
---@field Title? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList A finding's title.
---@field Description? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList A finding's description.
---@field RecommendationText? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The recommendation of what to do about the issue described in a finding.
---@field SourceUrl? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList A URL that links to a page about the current finding in the security findings provider's solution.
---@field ProductFields? aws.securityhub.MapFilterList A data type where security findings providers can include additional solution-specific details that aren't part of the defined AwsSecurityFinding format.
