---@field Sample? aws.securityhub.BooleanFilterList Indicates whether or not sample findings are included in the filter results.
---@field ComplianceSecurityControlId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The unique identifier of a control across standards. Values for this field typically consist of an Amazon Web Services service and a number, such as APIGateway.5.
---@field ComplianceAssociatedStandardsId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The unique identifier of a standard in which a control is enabled. This field consists of the resource portion of the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) returned for a standard in the DescribeStandards API response.
---@field VulnerabilitiesExploitAvailable? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList Indicates whether a software vulnerability in your environment has a known exploit. You can filter findings by this field only if you use Security Hub CSPM and Amazon Inspector.
---@field VulnerabilitiesFixAvailable? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList Indicates whether a vulnerability is fixed in a newer version of the affected software packages. You can filter findings by this field only if you use Security Hub CSPM and Amazon Inspector.
---@field ComplianceSecurityControlParametersName? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The name of a security control parameter.
---@field ComplianceSecurityControlParametersValue? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The current value of a security control parameter.
---@field AwsAccountName? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The name of the Amazon Web Services account in which a finding is generated.
---@field ResourceApplicationName? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The name of the application that is related to a finding.
---@field ResourceApplicationArn? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The ARN of the application that is related to a finding.
---@field ResourceOwnerAccountId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The unique identifier of the account that owns the resource that the finding applies to, for example, Azure Subscription Id or Amazon Web Services Account Id
---@field ResourceOwnerOrgId? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The unique identifier of the organization that owns the resource that the finding applies to, for example, Azure Tenant Id
---@field ResourceProvider? aws.securityhub.StringFilterList The cloud provider that the resource belongs to. Valid values are AWS and Azure.

