---@field AwsSageMakerNotebookInstance? aws.securityhub.AwsSageMakerNotebookInstanceDetails
---@field AwsWafv2WebAcl? aws.securityhub.AwsWafv2WebAclDetails
---@field AwsWafv2RuleGroup? aws.securityhub.AwsWafv2RuleGroupDetails
---@field AwsEc2RouteTable? aws.securityhub.AwsEc2RouteTableDetails Provides details about a route table. A route table contains a set of rules, called routes, that determine where to direct network traffic from your subnet or gateway.
---@field AwsAmazonMqBroker? aws.securityhub.AwsAmazonMqBrokerDetails Provides details about AppSync message broker. A message broker allows software applications and components to communicate using various programming languages, operating systems, and formal messaging protocols.
---@field AwsAppSyncGraphQlApi? aws.securityhub.AwsAppSyncGraphQlApiDetails Provides details about an AppSync Graph QL API, which lets you query multiple databases, microservices, and APIs from a single GraphQL endpoint.
---@field AwsEventSchemasRegistry? aws.securityhub.AwsEventSchemasRegistryDetails A schema defines the structure of events that are sent to Amazon EventBridge. Schema registries are containers for schemas. They collect and organize schemas so that your schemas are in logical groups.
---@field AwsGuardDutyDetector? aws.securityhub.AwsGuardDutyDetectorDetails Provides details about an Amazon GuardDuty detector. A detector is an object that represents the GuardDuty service. A detector is required for GuardDuty to become operational.
---@field AwsStepFunctionStateMachine? aws.securityhub.AwsStepFunctionStateMachineDetails Provides details about an Step Functions state machine, which is a workflow consisting of a series of event-driven steps.
---@field AwsAthenaWorkGroup? aws.securityhub.AwsAthenaWorkGroupDetails Provides information about an Amazon Athena workgroup. A workgroup helps you separate users, teams, applications, or workloads. It also helps you set limits on data processing and track costs.
---@field AwsEventsEventbus? aws.securityhub.AwsEventsEventbusDetails Provides details about Amazon EventBridge event bus for an endpoint. An event bus is a router that receives events and delivers them to zero or more destinations, or targets.
---@field AwsDmsEndpoint? aws.securityhub.AwsDmsEndpointDetails Provides details about an Database Migration Service (DMS) endpoint. An endpoint provides connection, data store type, and location information about your data store.
---@field AwsEventsEndpoint? aws.securityhub.AwsEventsEndpointDetails Provides details about an Amazon EventBridge global endpoint. The endpoint can improve your application’s availability by making it Regional-fault tolerant.
---@field AwsDmsReplicationTask? aws.securityhub.AwsDmsReplicationTaskDetails Provides details about an DMS replication task. A replication task moves a set of data from the source endpoint to the target endpoint.
---@field AwsDmsReplicationInstance? aws.securityhub.AwsDmsReplicationInstanceDetails Provides details about an DMS replication instance. DMS uses a replication instance to connect to your source data store, read the source data, and format the data for consumption by the target data store.
---@field AwsRoute53HostedZone? aws.securityhub.AwsRoute53HostedZoneDetails Provides details about an Amazon Route 53 hosted zone, including the four name servers assigned to the hosted zone. A hosted zone represents a collection of records that can be managed together, belonging to a single parent domain name.
---@field AwsMskCluster? aws.securityhub.AwsMskClusterDetails Provides details about an Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) cluster.
---@field AwsS3AccessPoint? aws.securityhub.AwsS3AccessPointDetails Provides details about an Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) access point. S3 access points are named network endpoints that are attached to S3 buckets that you can use to perform S3 object operations.
---@field AwsEc2ClientVpnEndpoint? aws.securityhub.AwsEc2ClientVpnEndpointDetails Provides details about an Client VPN endpoint. A Client VPN endpoint is the resource that you create and configure to enable and manage client VPN sessions. It's the termination point for all client VPN sessions.
---@field CodeRepository? aws.securityhub.CodeRepositoryDetails Details about an external code repository with which you can connect your Amazon Web Services resources. The connection is established through Amazon Inspector.
