---Provides comprehensive details about an Amazon Web Services resource and its associated security findings.
---@class aws.securityhub.ResourceResult
---@field ResourceGuid? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The global identifier used to identify a resource.
---@field ResourceId aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The unique identifier for a resource.
---@field AccountId aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The Amazon Web Services account that recorded the resource data in Security Hub.
---@field AccountName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the Amazon Web Services account that's associated with the resource.
---@field Region aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The Amazon Web Services Region that recorded the resource data in Security Hub.
---@field ResourceProvider? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The cloud provider where the resource exists. Valid values are AWS and Azure. This field is always included.
---@field ResourceOwnerAccountId? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The identifier of the cloud account that owns the resource. For Amazon Web Services resources, this is the Amazon Web Services account ID. For Azure resources, this is the Azure subscription ID.
---@field ResourceOwnerOrgId? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The identifier of the cloud organization that owns the resource. For Amazon Web Services resources, this is the Organizations ID. For Azure resources, this is the Azure tenant ID.
---@field ResourceCloudPartition? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The cloud partition where the resource exists. For Amazon Web Services, valid values include aws, aws-cn, and aws-us-gov. This field isn't returned for cloud providers that don't use partitions.
---@field ResourceRegion? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The native cloud region where the resource is located. For Amazon Web Services, this is an Amazon Web Services Region (for example, us-east-1). For Azure resources, this is the Azure region (for example, westus2). This field is always included.
---@field ResourceCategory? aws.securityhub.ResourceCategory The grouping where the resource belongs.
---@field ResourceType aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The type of resource.
---@field ResourceName? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The name of the resource.
---@field ResourceCreationTimeDt? aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The time when the resource was created.
---@field ResourceDetailCaptureTimeDt aws.securityhub.NonEmptyString The timestamp when information about the resource was captured.
---@field FindingsSummary? aws.securityhub.ResourceFindingsSummaryList An aggregated view of security findings associated with a resource.
---@field ResourceTags? aws.securityhub.ResourceTagList The key-value pairs associated with a resource.
---@field ResourceConfig aws.securityhub.ResourceConfig The configuration details of a resource.
---@field ResourceSubCategory? aws.securityhub.ResourceSubCategory The AI/ML sub-grouping of the resource. Present only when ResourceCategory is AI/ML.
---@field DiscoveryType? aws.securityhub.DiscoveryType Specifies how the resource was discovered. If the value is Managed, the resource is natively provided by a cloud service provider. If the value is SelfHosted, the resource is hosted on customer-managed infrastructure, such as a compute instance or container image.
---@field ResourceInfo? aws.securityhub.ResourceInfo Additional resource-type-specific details. For self-hosted AI resources and their host resources, contains an AIDetails structure.
---@field ResourceCriticality? aws.securityhub.ResourceCriticality The criticality assigned to a resource.
---@field CriticalitySources? aws.securityhub.CriticalitySourceList The sources of criticalities determined from a resource.

